Subject: The profile records what the live objects hold in every slot of a profiled shape

What this does
  - At the profile dump, a walk over the live objects adds one line per slot that held a value:
    `V <shape> <slot> types=<set> vs=<shapes> vm=<0|1>`. `types` is the union of the value kinds, `vs` lists up to four
    shape ids the object values had, and `vm` is set when there were more or a value has a shape that is not in the table.

Why we need it
  The generator derives what a contracted layout can promise about a slot (an int, an object of one layout) from it.
  The walk runs once, in the profile build, after the program has finished; no running path changes.

Functions touched
  `aot_dump_contents`, `aot_dump_profile`.

No.

